-`src/i18n/messages.js`. The server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (default `en`).
+`src/i18n/messages.js`; every error code has a message in both.
+
+The server answers in the language the request's `Accept-Language` header
+prefers: the supported language with the highest q-value (the first one
+listed on a tie). Region tags are ignored (`ko-KR` is `ko`, `en-US` is `en`)
+and a language with `q=0` is never chosen. Without the header, or when it
+names no supported language, the server answers in `LARDER_LANG` (`en` or
+`ko`, default `en`).
